---
title: "Quickstart"
description: "Create a Qdrant collection, upsert documents, and query them with the qql-rs CLI."
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

This path uses Qdrant REST on port `6333` and an OpenAI-compatible embedding
endpoint. If you already store vectors, omit the embedder and use vector input.

{% steps %}

1. Start Qdrant

   {% terminal title="Qdrant" %}
   docker run --rm -p 6333:6333 -p 6334:6334 qdrant/qdrant
   {% /terminal %}

2. Configure execution

   {% terminal title="Environment" %}
   export QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6333
   export EMBED_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1/embeddings
   export EMBED_MODEL=all-minilm:l6-v2
   export EMBED_DIM=384
   {% /terminal %}

3. Create a collection

   {% qqlExample title="Dense collection and filter index" %}
   ```sql
   CREATE COLLECTION docs (
     dense VECTOR(384, COSINE)
   ) WITH HNSW (m = 16, ef_construct = 100);

   CREATE INDEX ON COLLECTION docs FOR category TYPE keyword;
   ```
   {% /qqlExample %}

4. Upsert content

   {% qqlExample title="Embed text into the dense vector" %}
   ```sql
   UPSERT INTO docs VALUES
     {id: 1, text: 'QQL provides typed vector retrieval', category: 'qql'},
     {id: 2, text: 'Qdrant stores dense and sparse vectors', category: 'qdrant'}
    USING DENSE MODEL 'all-minilm:l6-v2';
   ```
   {% /qqlExample %}

5. Search

   {% qqlExample title="Filtered search" %}
   ```sql
   QUERY TEXT 'typed query language' FROM docs
   USING dense
    WHERE category = 'qql'
    LIMIT 5;
   ```
   {% /qqlExample %}

{% /steps %}

Save the statements as `quickstart.qql`, then execute the whole script:

{% terminal title="Execute the script" %}
qql execute quickstart.qql
{% /terminal %}

Use `qql explain "QUERY ..."` to inspect a plan without sending it to Qdrant.
